From 313efa0073e9cd45681032e018647930dbf52bed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 23:32:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2492/3799] soh: rename func_800F314C -> Audio_SetMainBgmIoPort

Name source: DEDUCED from the code (confidence GUESS) -- zeldaret/oot
leaves this symbol address-named too, so there is no upstream name to adopt.
Reason: queues an 0x82 command on the main BGM player with the argument in the port byte and a value of 1; the port's meaning is not established
Defined in soh/src/code/audio_general.c.

Tagged [LLM:GUESS] at the definition, every declaration and every call site, so a
reader meeting the name anywhere knows it is inferred.
---
 soh/src/code/audio_general.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/soh/src/code/audio_general.c b/soh/src/code/audio_general.c
index 08c2691e0..a02df8bd7 100644
--- a/soh/src/code/audio_general.c
+++ b/soh/src/code/audio_general.c
@@ -3955,7 +3955,8 @@ void Audio_Noop1(UNK_TYPE arg0) {
 void Audio_Noop2(UNK_TYPE arg0, UNK_TYPE arg1) {
 }
 
-void func_800F314C(s8 arg0) {
+// LLM generated name (GUESS), was func_800F314C: queues an 0x82 command on the main BGM player with the argument in the port byte and a value of 1; the port's meaning is not established
+void Audio_SetMainBgmIoPort(s8 arg0) {
     Audio_QueueCmdS32(0x82 << 24 | SEQ_PLAYER_BGM_MAIN << 16 | (((u8)arg0 & 0xFF) << 8), 1);
 }
 
